# examples/asn1/enum_ext.asn1 in the ALIGNED variant. Found by
# byte mutation, derived by hand from X.691 (02/2021) 14.3, 11.6: an
# extension value's index is a normally small non-negative whole number.
#
# Grown ::= ENUMERATED {a, b, c, ..., d-v1700, e-v1700}: 1 (extension), then
# 1: 11.6.2's long form, which is for n >= 64; padding, length 1, 00: index
# 0 = d-v1700, which 11.6.1 puts in the short form, 0 000000 (80).
reject! Grown c00100  # asn1c, rasn, pycrate accept "d-v1700"
# the same, length 2, 0000: and not the minimum octets either (11.7.4, 11.3.6)
reject! Grown c0020000  # asn1c, rasn, pycrate accept "d-v1700"
# Lone ::= ENUMERATED {only, ...}: 1, 0 000000: extension index 0, a newer
# version's value, which an ENUMERATED of this schema cannot hold, so ours
# rejects it (emit/enum_ext.rs; smallnum.vec's BigEnum is the same)
reject! Lone 80  # pycrate keeps it as "_ext_0"; asn1c -c and rasn reject it too
